                        @* Section 1 *@
                        <div class="br-section" id="s1">
                            <h2 class="br-h2">1. Why Traders Lose Even with a Good Strategy</h2>
                            <p class="br-p">Studies consistently show that the majority of retail forex traders lose money — not because their strategies are wrong, but because their position sizing is inconsistent. A strategy with a 55% win rate and a 1:2 risk-reward ratio is mathematically profitable. But if you risk 10% on one trade and 0.5% on the next, the math breaks down entirely.</p>
                            <p class="br-p">The position size calculator removes emotion from the equation. Instead of guessing how many lots "feels right", you calculate exactly how many lots keep your risk at a fixed, predetermined percentage of your account — every single trade, without exception.</p>

                            <div class="br-pros-cons">
                                <div class="br-pros">
                                    <div class="br-pros-title"><i class="fa-solid fa-circle-check me-2"></i>Traders Who Use Position Sizing</div>
                                    <ul style="margin:0;padding:0 0 0 18px;line-height:2.2;font-size:14px;color:#374151;">
                                        <li>Risk is consistent — strategy edge plays out over time</li>
                                        <li>Losing streaks are survivable and expected</li>
                                        <li>Account grows proportionally with the balance</li>
                                        <li>Psychology improves — no single trade is "make or break"</li>
                                        <li>Performance is measurable and improvable</li>
                                    </ul>
                                </div>
                                <div class="br-cons">
                                    <div class="br-cons-title"><i class="fa-solid fa-circle-xmark me-2"></i>Traders Who Guess Lot Sizes</div>
                                    <ul style="margin:0;padding:0 0 0 18px;line-height:2.2;font-size:14px;color:#374151;">
                                        <li>One large loss can wipe out weeks of gains</li>
                                        <li>"High confidence" trades lead to over-leveraging</li>
                                        <li>Impossible to evaluate if the strategy actually works</li>
                                        <li>Emotional decisions after losses compound the damage</li>
                                        <li>Even profitable strategies eventually blow the account</li>
                                    </ul>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>

                        <div class="br-divider"></div>

                        @* Section 2 — 6-Step Routine *@
                        <div class="br-section" id="s2">
                            <h2 class="br-h2">2. Your 6-Step Pre-Trade Position Sizing Routine</h2>
                            <p class="br-p">Make this workflow non-negotiable before every trade. It takes less than 60 seconds and ensures your risk is calculated correctly every time — not estimated, not guessed.</p>

